# gate) are measured in worker/tests/test_generator_slots.cpp. The harness can
# only subset-match, so ABSENCE of `generatorSlot` is shown behaviourally: a
# slotted ref on a legacy body falls back to the ordinary pool.
#   ROUND 1 — V3 rect extrude `op1` (regionIdentityVersion 3), ACCEPTED.
#   ROUND 2 — AcquireElementIds on its top +x edge returns the LITERAL
#             descriptor.generatorSlot {recordId op1, slot "edge:cap:+|side:e1"}.
#   ROUND 3 — ResolveRefs, gate OPEN: a ref carrying that slot whose anchor
#             sits on the congruent BOTTOM edge autoBinds the slotted top edge
#             (e:4). The same ref without the slot is a NeedsRepair tie.
#   ROUND 4 — a LEGACY rect (`op3`) and a LEGACY circle (`op5`), no
#             regionIdentityVersion, ACCEPTED. Their edges are acquired without
#             a slot, and the same slotted ref (their own record id) is NOT
#             narrowed: NeedsRepair, as with no slot at all.
#   ROUND 5 — TransformBody on `body_op1` erases its provenance (gate CLOSED);
#             the slotted ref of ROUND 3 now falls back to the ordinary pool
#             and is NeedsRepair.
